---
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
import BaseLayoutV2 from '../layouts/BaseLayoutV2.astro';
import EmailCaptureForm from '../components/EmailCaptureForm.tsx';

const stages = [
  { n: '01', name: 'Frame', body: 'Clarify the actual mandate, decision owner, stakes, desired outcome and criteria for a good call.' },
  { n: '02', name: 'Inspect', body: 'Separate evidence from interpretation, surface contradictions and identify the assumptions or unknowns carrying the decision.' },
  { n: '03', name: 'Test', body: 'Form a working hypothesis, challenge it against alternatives and make explicit what evidence could change the view.' },
  { n: '04', name: 'Compare', body: 'Develop genuinely distinct options and assess them consistently against the decision scorecard.' },
  { n: '05', name: 'Decide', body: 'Make a traceable recommendation when the evidence permits, or define the evidence-producing decision required before committing.' },
  { n: '06', name: 'Execute', body: 'Translate the call into proportionate action, ownership, measures, decision thresholds and review conditions.' },
];
---
<BaseLayoutV2
  title="How GreenSquare works | Professional judgement for AI"
  description="GreenSquare gives capable AI a disciplined professional judgement process: frame the mandate, inspect evidence, test assumptions, compare options, decide and execute."
  current="product"
>
  <section class="v-section v-off hero">
    <div class="v-container">
      <div class="v-split is-top">
        <div class="v-reveal">
          <h1 class="v-display">The model provides intelligence. GreenSquare controls how it is applied.</h1>
          <p class="v-lead" style="margin-top: var(--v-6);">
            Capable AI can research, analyse and write at speed. GreenSquare adds the professional judgement layer:
            what should be clarified first, what evidence is sufficient, which assumptions deserve challenge, which
            options are real and when the work is ready for a call.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="v-btn v-btn--green" href={withBase('/decision-frame/')}>Get the free Decision Frame</a>
            <a class="v-btn v-btn--grey" href={withBase('/benchmark/')}>Review the evidence</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="v-reveal d1">
          <div class="v-readout">
            <div class="v-readout__bar"><span class="v-readout__dot"></span> Decision Frame V2</div>
            <div class="v-readout__body">
              <ul class="v-spec__list">
                {stages.map((stage) => <li><span class="n">{Number(stage.n)}</span> {stage.name}</li>)}
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="v-readout__foot">One portable method / depth scales with the stakes</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section">
    <div class="v-container">
      <h2 class="v-h2" style="max-width: 25ch;">Give the AI the problem, not a carefully engineered prompt.</h2>
      <div class="decision-grid" style="margin-top: var(--v-8);">
        <ul class="v-leadlist v-reveal">
          <li><strong>Strategic choices.</strong> Markets, investments, partnerships and material operating-model decisions.</li>
          <li><strong>Portfolio choices.</strong> Prioritisation, funding, sequencing and trade-offs across competing initiatives.</li>
        </ul>
        <ul class="v-leadlist v-reveal d1">
          <li><strong>Transformation decisions.</strong> Scope, vendors, timing, capability, benefits and course correction.</li>
          <li><strong>Operating decisions.</strong> Hiring, pricing, capacity, process, products and other calls where plausible advice is not enough.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-fill">
    <div class="v-container">
      <h2 class="v-h2">A repeatable reasoning loop, not a fixed questionnaire.</h2>
      <div class="v-caplist">
        {stages.map((stage, index) => (
          <div class={`v-caprow v-reveal${index > 0 ? ` d${Math.min(index, 3)}` : ''}`}>
            <span class="v-index">State {Number(stage.n)}</span>
            <h3>{stage.name}</h3>
            <p class="v-small v-cap-body">{stage.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section">
    <div class="v-container v-split is-top">
      <div class="v-reveal">
        <h2 class="v-h2">The decision remains inspectable.</h2>
        <p class="v-measure" style="margin-top: var(--v-5); color: var(--v-ink-soft);">
          GreenSquare does not ask the user to trust a polished answer. Material evidence, assumptions, unresolved
          gaps, decision criteria, trade-offs and conditions for changing course stay visible through the process.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="v-reveal d1">
        <div class="v-readout">
          <div class="v-readout__bar"><span class="v-readout__dot"></span> Evidence state</div>
          <div class="v-readout__body">
            <ul class="v-spec__list">
              <li><span class="n">1</span> GIVEN</li>
              <li><span class="n">2</span> DERIVED</li>
              <li><span class="n">3</span> INFERRED</li>
              <li><span class="n">4</span> UNKNOWN</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-green">
    <div class="v-container v-split">
      <div class="v-reveal">
        <h2 class="v-h2">Use the AI environment you already have.</h2>
        <p class="v-lead" style="margin-top: var(--v-5);">
          The Decision Frame is a portable file. GreenSquare does not need access to the decision in order for the
          method to run inside the user's chosen AI environment.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="v-reveal d1">
        <ul class="v-leadlist">
          <li><strong>Nothing to install.</strong> Upload the file and give the model the business problem.</li>
          <li><strong>Model-agnostic direction.</strong> The method is designed to sit above changing foundation models.</li>
          <li><strong>User accountability.</strong> Assumptions, evidence and uncertainty remain available for professional challenge.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-fill">
    <div class="v-container v-container--narrow">
      <h2 class="v-h2">The evidence boundary is explicit.</h2>
      <p class="v-measure" style="margin-top: var(--v-5); color: var(--v-ink-soft);">
        GreenSquare publishes its current benchmark because process compliance and better judgement are not the same
        claim. The existing evidence shows where the method changes model behaviour and where further real-user
        evidence is still required.
      </p>
      <a class="v-link" href={withBase('/benchmark/')} style="display:inline-block; margin-top: var(--v-5);">Review the results and limitations</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-green" id="get-started">
    <div class="v-container v-split is-top">
      <div class="v-reveal">
        <h2 class="v-h2">Use the current GreenSquare decision system free.</h2>
        <p class="v-lead" style="margin-top: var(--v-5);">
          Decision Frame V2 is the current free product candidate: a complete adaptive decision experience designed
          to take a capable model from the mandate through evidence, options, recommendation and proportionate execution.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="v-reveal d1">
        <div class="v-card">
          <EmailCaptureForm client:visible buttonLabel="Email me the Decision Frame" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section">
    <div class="v-container v-container--narrow">
      <h2 class="v-h2">Common questions.</h2>
      <div style="margin-top: var(--v-8);">
        <details open>
          <summary>What exactly is the Decision Frame?</summary>
          <p class="v-small">A portable operating method for a capable AI model. It controls how the conversation frames, interrogates, tests and advances a business decision.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need to install anything?</summary>
          <p class="v-small">No. Upload the file to your chosen capable AI model and describe the decision or business problem in your own words.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which AI services can I use?</summary>
          <p class="v-small">The product is designed for capable versions of ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini. The launch compatibility note will identify the versions actually tested for the locked release.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does GreenSquare make the decision for me?</summary>
          <p class="v-small">No. It improves the process by which the call is reached and makes the evidence, assumptions, uncertainty and trade-offs more inspectable. The user remains accountable for the decision.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What will GreenSquare charge for next?</summary>
          <p class="v-small">The next paid professional job will be determined from how people use the free product and what repeated work they value. GreenSquare is not withholding arbitrary parts of the current method to manufacture an upgrade.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayoutV2>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(3rem, 6vh, 5rem); }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; gap: var(--v-4); align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: var(--v-8); }
  .decision-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--v-8); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .decision-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--v-4); } }
</style>
